{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774527342,"nonce":"Z2O39JMfvAKjfaLDHg/6uxXY9tk=","title":"Streaming loss: compute loss inside lax.scan to eliminate trajectory storage","message":"Sub-issue of 3ef9c25 (memory-efficient training umbrella).\n\nAdd streaming_loss_fn parameter to iterate_component and run_component in iterate.py. When provided, the scan accumulates a scalar loss instead of storing state_history.\n\nCreate feedbax/streaming_loss.py with a helper that constructs a per-step streaming loss function from a CompositeLoss + trial_specs + model. The helper precomputes targets and time weights for each TargetStateLoss term, so the scan body only needs the current state and timestep index.\n\nNon-streamable loss types (StopAtGoalLoss, EffectorStraightPathLoss, etc.) raise NotImplementedError.","files":null}]}